From 68e74f667b4122b4c91c1a7a26fe3d0145a21762 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Michael Crowe <southwestfungi@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 31 Aug 2026 23:55:12 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] Crowe Sense writes into the Environment lane

The Cultivation space has promised since 0.8 that Crowe Sense would write
room readings into the same store the grower types into. sense.js is that
write: a poller reads a paired node (direct, the node's own API; or cloud,
the relay with the Crowe ID bearer) once a minute and upserts one env row
per room per UTC hour, marked source crowe-sense, so an hour's row is
rewritten rather than stacked. The store honours a caller-supplied id only
for the sense: prefix; everything else keeps the old rule that an id must
already exist.

The lane marks those rows measured, the Overview gets a Crowe Sense card
(paired or not, ok, stale or down, age of the last reading), and its footnote
says which rows an instrument wrote once one has. Settings gains Source,
Node URL and Node id, placed below Guardrails so the space checkboxes stay
where test-panels hit-tests them.

Contract: crowe-sense/contracts/telemetry-v1.md. The web and mobile bridges
grow the same sense.{status,configure,onChange} surface (cloud only; a
browser tab and a phone have no route to a node's plain-http API), so the
parity walks hold. scripts/test-sense.js covers the endpoint resolution, the
mapper, staleness and the poller in plain node.

